From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:05:38 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Add SM6450 USB3/DP PHY
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The USB3 and DisplayPort combo PHY on SM6450 is SM8350's: the same
register layout, and the downstream tree's init sequence writes the
same 152 registers SM8350's configuration does, none missing and none
extra. It agrees on 144 of the values. The other eight are receiver
tuning: UCDR_FO_GAIN, UCDR_SO_GAIN and SIGDET_CNTRL on both lanes,
and the PCS's LOCK_DETECT_CONFIG1 and 2. Add RX and PCS tables with
those values and SM8350's configuration otherwise.

The DisplayPort half follows SM8350 too. Downstream gives it the same
PHY version, 4.2, and the AUX settings qmp_v4_dp_aux_init() writes.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 109 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 109 insertions(+)

